 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? Keep it in the back of a refrigerator, where you can see it through the door open, it's the coldest spot in most homes. Filling it with cold food also helps. Blocks are the classic way, you stack them in the hole with a little bit of vegetable oil, and they stay cold for days. Put the coldest things at the top, so you reach them first and they stay freshest. Keep an open container of cold salad on top, and eat through it first. Then keep hot drinks out of it, and keep the coldest things out of reach of little ones. Yes, pour it down the sink each morning, or it ices the inside.",
